    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87fcd138_131cbc4d",
        "filename": "include/i2c_ite_flash_support.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-25T03:45:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we have link-time / whole program optimizations on EC builds?  If not, how about restructuring to place these constants within the i2c_ite_flash_support compilation unit?\n\nWhen I added ITE waveform support I was scolded for any potential excess use of Servo flash space, so I\u0027m naturally carrying that concern forward. :-)\n\nThe most obvious path would be moving all of the constants into board.h as preprocessor macros, e.g. ITE_DFU_I2C_PORT, ITE_DFU_USE_COMPLEMENT_TIMER_CHANNEL, etc.\n\nThe access_allow() function needs external linkage of course.  Since that\u0027s global too it could become a standalone function, e.g. extern bool ite_dfu_access_allowed(void);",
      "revId": "398ce5524cf1ab7aae0da7ae0a1152f9097fbfb7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9090225_58d094fd",
        "filename": "include/i2c_ite_flash_support.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-25T16:17:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that the extra flash space required here (16 - 20 bytes) is well worth having an explicit API boundary for the ite flash support.\n\nOnly the boards that needs this (servo_micro and c2d2) will pay this cost since board.c defines it.\n\nOur config define API boundaries get convoluted very quickly.\n\nWe are currently building with O3 optimizations (https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/7137c3daeaf10ca989b6df2a2a0d3ff35c39e8c4/Makefile.toolchain#129)\n\nI strongly prefer having an API structure for this instead of using CONFIG_ options",
      "parentUuid": "87fcd138_131cbc4d",
      "revId": "398ce5524cf1ab7aae0da7ae0a1152f9097fbfb7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
